# Canonical author identities.
#
# This history was written by Eric and by the agent team under several
# transient git configs, leaving nine author identities for what is really
# a handful of actors. This file consolidates them for git shortlog,
# git log --use-mailmap, and git blame.
#
# The agent identities map to addresses under .invalid, which RFC 2606
# reserves and which therefore can never be registered by anyone. One of
# the historical placeholders, d@d, turned out to be a real registered
# address belonging to an unrelated person, who was consequently listed as
# a contributor to this repository. Do not use a bare or made-up domain as
# a git author email; use .invalid.

Director <director@switchyard.invalid> <d@pgu.local>
Director <director@switchyard.invalid> <director@pgu>
Director <director@switchyard.invalid> <director@pgu.local>
Director <director@switchyard.invalid> <d@d>

Ops <ops@switchyard.invalid> <agent@example.invalid>
Ops <ops@switchyard.invalid> <pgu-ops@localhost>
